    {
      "id": "operator-graph-norm-completeness",
      "type": "exercise",
      "regions": [
        [
          250,
          80,
          1025,
          955,
          1325
        ]
      ],
      "en": "For any linear operator $(\\mathcal{D}(A),A)$ from $X$ to $Y$ we define the \\textbf{graph norm} on $\\mathcal{D}(A)\\subset X$ by\\[\\|x\\|_G:=\\|x\\|_X+\\|A(x)\\|_Y\\quad\\text{for any }x\\in\\mathcal{D}(A).\\]\\begin{enumerate}[label=(\\alph*)]\\item Show that this does indeed define a norm on $\\mathcal{D}(A)$.\\item Show that $(\\mathcal{D}(A),A)$ is closed if and only if $\\mathcal{D}(A)$ equipped with the graph norm is a Banach space.\\item Every normed linear space has a completion (hence $\\mathcal{D}(A)$ equipped with the graph norm does as well) yet not every operator is closable. Why is this not a contradiction?\\end{enumerate}",
      "zh": "对于从 $X$ 到 $Y$ 的任意线性算子 $(\\mathcal{D}(A),A)$, 用下式在 $\\mathcal{D}(A)\\subset X$ 上定义\\textbf{图范数}:\\[\\|x\\|_G:=\\|x\\|_X+\\|A(x)\\|_Y\\quad\\text{for any }x\\in\\mathcal{D}(A).\\]\\begin{enumerate}[label=(\\alph*)]\\item 证明这确实定义了 $\\mathcal{D}(A)$ 上的一个范数.\\item 证明, $(\\mathcal{D}(A),A)$ 是闭的, 当且仅当赋予图范数的 $\\mathcal{D}(A)$ 是 Banach 空间.\\item 每个赋范线性空间都有完备化 (因而赋予图范数的 $\\mathcal{D}(A)$ 也有完备化), 但并非每个算子都是可闭的. 为什么这并不矛盾?\\end{enumerate}",
      "label": "ex:operator-graph-norm-completeness",
      "render_role": "exercise",
      "source_locations": [
        {
          "pdf_page": 250,
          "printed_page": 240,
          "bbox": [
            31.98712273641851,
            409.94829760403536,
