    {
      "id": "relative-bound-closed-operator-sum",
      "type": "exercise",
      "regions": [
        [
          251,
          80,
          245,
          955,
          415
        ]
      ],
      "en": "Let $A$ and $B$ be operators from $X$ to $Y$. We say that $B$ is bounded relative to $A$ if $\\mathcal{D}(B)\\supseteq\\mathcal{D}(A)$ and there exists $a,b>0$ such that\\[\\|Bx\\|_Y\\leq a\\|Ax\\|_Y+b\\|x\\|_X\\]for every $x\\in\\mathcal{D}(A)$. Prove the following: If $A$ is closed and $B$ is bounded relative to $A$ with $a<1$, then $A+B$ (with domain $\\mathcal{D}(A)$) is closed.",
      "zh": "设 $A$ 和 $B$ 为从 $X$ 到 $Y$ 的算子. 若 $\\mathcal{D}(B)\\supseteq\\mathcal{D}(A)$, 且存在 $a,b>0$, 使得对于每个 $x\\in\\mathcal{D}(A)$ 均有\\[\\|Bx\\|_Y\\leq a\\|Ax\\|_Y+b\\|x\\|_X\\]则称 $B$ 相对于 $A$ 有界. 证明以下结果: 若 $A$ 是闭的, 且 $B$ 相对于 $A$ 有界, 其中 $a<1$, 则 $A+B$ (定义域为 $\\mathcal{D}(A)$) 是闭的.",
      "label": "ex:relative-bound-closed-operator-sum",
      "render_role": "exercise",
      "source_locations": [
